abstract: >
  SIRIUS LOCAL AI is a fully modular, offline-only AI runtime designed for secure,
  deterministic execution of commands, workflows, plugins, reasoning tasks, and
  semantic automation. Version 5.7.0 finalizes the stabilized logic layer of the
  Unified Runtime Architecture 5.x, delivering a fully unified Knowledge Graph,
  deep explainability (KG_EXPLAIN & KG_EXPLAIN_DEEP), multi-hop inference,
  inheritance reasoning, transitive reasoning, proof tree generation, evidence
  trees, confidence scoring, and deterministic rule chaining.

  The Unified Runtime Architecture 5.7.0 merges PC and Mobile logic into a single,
  deterministic, identity-aware operating layer. Runtime Core 5.7.0 provides unified
  orchestration, deterministic execution, capability-based access control,
  identity-aware routing, and explainability-aware workflow dispatch.

  SECURITY FAMILY 5.x expands identity and family safety layers with OWNER/FAMILY/
  STRANGER identity levels, time-limits v3, safe-mode for unknown users, and a
  Schoolwork Engine ensuring unrestricted access to academic tasks.

  The system operates entirely on the user's device, without any cloud dependencies
  or external data transmission. All modules follow strict security boundaries,
  deterministic behavior, semantic understanding, explainability, and predictable
  execution rules.

  Version 5.7.0 upgrades the entire runtime stack, including Workflow Engine 5.7.0,
  Reasoning Engine 5.7.0, KG_EXPLAIN, KG_EXPLAIN_DEEP, ENVOY 5, FS‑AGENT 5, CME‑MEM 5,
  System Agent 5, and Password Vault 5.0. These upgrades prepare the architecture
  for the upcoming Modular Kernel Architecture in the 5.x → 6.0 transition.
